    <sys:String x:Key="Tools.Compliance">Compliance &amp; licensing</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tools.DirectoryHint">"Install directory" is where the package manager keeps its packages; "CLI" is the probed command-line tool path and version.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tools.Disclaimer">UMango is an independent third-party application and is not affiliated with PCL / PCL-CE or its developers.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tools.DesignReference">The UI is modelled on PCL-CE; this project does not copy its source code, XAML or image assets;</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tools.AdoptedCode">Adopted PCL-CE code is limited to the Apache-2.0 licensed PCL.Core, annotated per file with origin and changes.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tools.Notice">See THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md in the repository for the full notice, per-file origin and change notes; the Apache-2.0 text is at https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tools.ProjectIntro">UMango is a cross-platform package manager GUI: npm / pnpm / Git / Scoop / WinGet / Homebrew in one window, with per-download-method step progress, live terminal output, and a record of every install/uninstall/upgrade.&#x0a;Built on .NET 10 + WPF; the business layer (UMango.Core) is UI-agnostic and reached only through its public API.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tools.IconLicense">UI icons use lucide (ISC licensed).</sys:String>

